WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.116
The analysis uses stochastic approximation,

00:00:03.196 --> 00:00:06.759
treating each algorithm as a noisy gradient flow.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.955
A stability lemma bounds the expected loss.

00:00:10.035 --> 00:00:12.557
Instead of uniformly bounded noise,

00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:19.842
they bound it relative to the loss. mSGD uses
decreasing Robbins-Monro steps with static momentum;

00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:22.890
AdaGrad's adaptive step needs new bounds.
